=== Adaptor cost: NIST ML-DSA vs the LAS paper's simplified Dilithium ===
build: commit aa71cbf branch report | ML-DSA-87 vs Simplified Dilithium-III (n=8, l=7, kappa=60)
protocol: 5 repetitions x 500 (sign-class) / 1000 (verify-class) iterations, mean +/- SD, same process

--- run-validity gates (a failure invalidates every timing above) ---
rejection gate [simplified Dilithium: Algorithm 1 Sign]: 2500 calls, measured 2.6916 attempts/call (acceptance 37.15%) vs exact theory 2.7186 (36.78%), 5-sigma tolerance +-0.2162 => OK
rejection gate [simplified Dilithium: Algorithm 2 PreSign]: 2500 calls, measured 2.7988 attempts/call (acceptance 35.73%) vs exact theory 2.7643 (36.18%), 5-sigma tolerance +-0.2208 => OK
rejection gate [ML-DSA: Sign (matched, no statement)]: 2500 calls, measured 3.9572 attempts/call (acceptance 25.27%) vs FIPS 204 published 3.8500 (25.97%), 5-sigma tolerance +-0.3312 => OK
rejection gate [ML-DSA: PreSign (adaptor)]: 2500 calls, measured 3.8676 attempts/call (acceptance 25.86%) vs FIPS 204 published 3.8500 (25.97%), 5-sigma tolerance +-0.3312 => OK

--- per-operation timing (us/op, mean +/- SD over 5 repetitions) ---
  operation  Simplified Dilithium-III              ML-DSA-87 ML-DSA/simp
  KeyGen              75.41 +/-  3.81         169.40 +/-  7.23      2.25x
  Sign               525.72 +/-  2.91         585.64 +/-  6.85      1.11x
  Verify             149.54 +/-  3.30         173.10 +/-  0.13      1.16x
  PreSign            585.44 +/- 18.42         610.01 +/- 15.36      1.04x
  PreVerify          153.62 +/-  2.73         180.98 +/-  0.41      1.18x
  Adapt              165.10 +/-  5.25         188.93 +/-  0.64      1.14x
  Extract             65.09 +/-  0.63         158.74 +/-  2.05      2.44x
  (ML-DSA Sign row is the MATCHED partner; stock crypto_sign_signature
   measured 571.82 +/- 25.20 us in the same run)

--- sign-class cost per ATTEMPT (rejection luck divided out) ---
                             Simplified Dilithium-III            ML-DSA-87
  Sign, us/attempt                    195.32 +/-  0.51      148.01 +/-  1.05
  PreSign, us/attempt                 209.27 +/-  4.03      157.79 +/-  2.81

--- adaptor overhead WITHIN each construction (the primary comparison) ---
  pair                       Simplified Dilithium-III            ML-DSA-87
  PreSign vs Sign (per attempt)                     7.1%                 6.6%
  PreVerify vs Verify                            2.7%                 4.6%
  Adapt vs Verify                               10.4%                 9.1%
  PreSign vs Sign (per call)                    11.4%                 4.2%
  (Extract has no basic analogue in either construction. The per-attempt
   PreSign figure is the algorithmic one; the per-call figure additionally
   carries the difference in realised restart counts, which is why the two
   can disagree in sign at this sample size.)

--- rejection sampling (counted directly, never inferred) ---
                             Simplified Dilithium-III            ML-DSA-87
  attempts/Sign                                2.6916               3.9572
  attempts/PreSign                             2.7988               3.8676

--- communication (bytes on the wire) ---
  object                     Simplified Dilithium-III            ML-DSA-87      ratio
  public key                                     5888                 2592      0.44x
  signature                                      9184                 4627      0.50x
  pre-signature                                  9184                 4627      0.50x
  statement Y                                    5888                 5888      1.00x
  witness                                         960                  672      0.70x
  swap payload (sig + Y)                        15072                10515      0.70x

NOTE: this is a COST comparison between two engineering routes to the
same adaptor functionality. It is NOT a security comparison: the two
constructions have different parameters and different security
arguments, and neither is analysed here (out of scope).

OK: rejection gates, attempt-counter checks and success-path
    assertions all passed. Caveat: the two constructions are measured
    sequentially within one process, so intra-run drift is not
    controlled for.
